.TH mnnn-model 1  "mnnn-model 2.15.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-model \- Models: record tables you design (typed fields, references, constraints), changed by versioned migrations you preview, apply and roll back; and their records
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn model\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Models: record tables you design (typed fields, references, constraints), changed by versioned migrations you preview, apply and roll back; and their records
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
Fields are NAME:TYPE with constraints: text, int, real, bool, timestamp, json, or ref:MODEL
(a record of another model). A trailing ! means required. Constraints: required, unique,
index, default=V, choices=a|b, about="…"; to take one away: optional, \-unique, \-index,
\-default, \-choices, \-about.
.PP
Changes go to a draft; `plan` shows the migration (+ add, \- drop, ~ change), `apply` makes
it the next version, `history` lists versions and `rollback` applies an old design as a new
version. Steps that lose values ask first (\-y says yes). The built\-in bars model is edited
the same way: its fields from imports can be renamed, retyped, changed or dropped (the bars
keep their imported values; rollback brings a dropped field back).
.PP
Examples:
  mnnn model create signals \-\-fields "symbol:text!; price:real!; side:text choices=buy|sell"
  mnnn model edit signals \-\-add "note:text" \-\-change "price:real default=0" \-\-apply
  mnnn model plan signals
  mnnn model rollback signals 1
  mnnn model record create signals symbol=BTC/USDT price=42000 side=buy
  mnnn model record list signals \-\-where "price > 40000" \-\-sort \-price
  mnnn model record list signals \-\-group side \-\-agg avg:price
  mnnn model record update signals \-\-where "side = buy" note=checked
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-model\-list(1)
List models (the built\-in bars model too)
.TP
mnnn\-model\-types(1)
List the field types
.TP
mnnn\-model\-create(1)
Create a model (applied as v1 unless \-\-draft)
.TP
mnnn\-model\-edit(1)
Change a model\*(Aqs draft (renames, then changes, drops, adds and moves), its name or description. \-\-apply applies the draft right away
.TP
mnnn\-model\-show(1)
Show a model: fields, draft, records and rules
.TP
mnnn\-model\-plan(1)
Show what applying the draft would do
.TP
mnnn\-model\-apply(1)
Apply the draft as the next version (a migration). \-y allows losing values
.TP
mnnn\-model\-discard(1)
Throw the draft away
.TP
mnnn\-model\-history(1)
List the applied versions
.TP
mnnn\-model\-rollback(1)
Apply the design of an earlier version as the next version
.TP
mnnn\-model\-remove(1)
Remove a model and its records (rules living in it become standalone, off)
.TP
mnnn\-model\-record(1)
Records of a model: create, update, list, show, delete
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
